  "biography": {
    "plain_text": "Donald R. Diamond was an American property developer, investor and philanthropist who became one of southern Arizona’s largest private landowners. A former Wall Street commodities broker, he founded Diamond Ventures to manage real-estate development and private-equity investments. His family’s giving helped establish Tucson’s Diamond Children’s Medical Center and supported education, medical research and civic institutions.",
    "html": "<p>Donald R. Diamond was an American property developer, investor and philanthropist who became one of southern Arizona’s largest private landowners. A former Wall Street commodities broker, he founded Diamond Ventures to manage real-estate development and private-equity investments. His family’s giving helped establish Tucson’s Diamond Children’s Medical Center and supported education, medical research and civic institutions.</p>\r\n",
