  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Born in New York, Diamond studied at the University of Arizona and met his future wife, Joan, there. He first built a successful career as a Wall Street commodities broker, then returned to Arizona and accumulated extensive land holdings around Tucson. He founded Diamond Ventures in 1988 to give his property development and business investments a dedicated operating platform.\n\nDiamond’s portfolio grew across residential, commercial and industrial property, alongside private-equity interests. He also helped establish the Phoenix Suns and Arizona Diamondbacks sports franchises. After losing a daughter to complications related to asthma, Donald and Joan Diamond became major supporters of paediatric care and research. Their lead gift helped create Diamond Children’s Medical Center, anchoring a wider record of support for the University of Arizona and Tucson institutions.",
    "html": "<p>Born in New York, Diamond studied at the University of Arizona and met his future wife, Joan, there. He first built a successful career as a Wall Street commodities broker, then returned to Arizona and accumulated extensive land holdings around Tucson. He founded Diamond Ventures in 1988 to give his property development and business investments a dedicated operating platform.</p>\r\n<p>Diamond’s portfolio grew across residential, commercial and industrial property, alongside private-equity interests. He also helped establish the Phoenix Suns and Arizona Diamondbacks sports franchises. After losing a daughter to complications related to asthma, Donald and Joan Diamond became major supporters of paediatric care and research. Their lead gift helped create Diamond Children’s Medical Center, anchoring a wider record of support for the University of Arizona and Tucson institutions.</p>\r\n",
